  "historical_output_text": " As a child, I was a voracious collector of baseball cards. My parents had given me a small, worn box to hold my collection, and I took it with me everywhere. I loved the smell of the box, the feel of the cards when I held them, the thrill of finding a new card. I would count and re-count my cards, as if the number was somehow a measure of my worth. \n\nOne day, I decided to clean the box and cards. My fingers moved quickly, sorting and arranging, when suddenly I felt a sharp pain in my index finger. I had been pricked by a thorn from a card's protective sleeve. Blood welled up, and I stopped, staring at the small thorn and my bleeding finger. \n\nI realized I had been so focused on my collection, so obsessed with perfection and",
